### Relationships

## N

N is the first Disassembly Drone that Uzi met when she was searching for a missing piece of her railgun. Upon their initial encounter in the "PILOT", N attempts to kill Uzi, leading to a protracted fight that ends with her firing her railgun at him, temporarily decapitating him. Upon regenerating, a malfunction in his optical systems causes him to mistake Uzi for a Disassembly Drone.

He helps her heal from an injury he previously inflicted, after which she questions his team's blind faith in their leadership. As the episode progresses, events compel N to throw in his lot with the Worker Drones, helping Uzi save the colony from V and J.

However, despite seeing N as an ally in her goal to kill all humans, Uzi begins to see N in fear after watching Eldritch J seemingly kill her father. However, this fear eventually fades after her guilt becomes "active" upon seeing an incredibly poorly drawn interpretation of herself and N given to her by the latter.

## V

V and Uzi have a complex relationship filled with ironic animosity and wariness, yet eventually trust and somewhat friendliness. V was originally hostile to Uzi, seeing her as nothing more than another one of her prey she was sent to devour. In "The Promening", she and Uzi do not see eye to eye much, although they seem to be temporarily at an understanding.

During the events of "Cabin Fever", V begins to see the importance Uzi has to N but disregards it, stating Uzi would have to be her next victim. After seeing that she was a host of the Absolute Solver and her infection was getting worse, V does not hesitate to attempt to dispatch her. When she is saved from being stabbed with her own dismembered tail by N, he tells her that he should have listened to him about not antagonizing Uzi.

In "Dead End", V starts to become concerned about Uzi when the Solver was attempting to take full control of her, and goes as far as saving her and preventing her from using her Solver powers so she doesn't get possessed. When V was surrounded by the Sentinels, she tells Uzi that she trusts her in taking care of N, then proceeds to cut off the wires of the elevator, sacrificing herself.

